// guarded). Every flagged (92) segment whose flagged pass fell back is counted and its reason line printed (<= 8 per arm) in every
// mode; ON a TRANSLATED fallback carrying a draw with RECTLIST in force is refused here (VERIFY / XLAT12_RFB_REFUSED), after rect92's
// own backstop and before the copy guard, exactly as rect92_seg refuses. `gRectFbSeg[k]` marks this pass's kept RECTLIST fallbacks
// (zeroed at the top of every policy pass) so a COMMITTED frame carrying one is counted (rectfb_commit). It writes no register, no
// page table and nothing of Apple's.
static volatile uint32_t gRectFbMode { N48_RFB_M_OFF };
static n48_rfb_st gRectFbS {};
